# Deploy from Cursor

## Flow

1. **Push to GitHub** → Vercel auto-deploys (when repo is connected)
2. **Production branch**: `clean-main`
3. **Site**: www.jobpool.in (after domain is configured in Vercel)

## When user says "deploy" or "push and deploy"

Run the deploy script from the repo root:
```bash
./scripts/deploy.sh "your commit message"
```
Or, if they prefer manual steps:
```bash
git add -A && git status
git commit -m "Brief description of changes"
git push origin clean-main
```

## Prerequisites

- Vercel project connected to `infojobpool/joshua-jpfrontend` on GitHub
- Root Directory in Vercel set to `app`
- Git credentials working (HTTPS or SSH)

## Admin app (`admin-temp`) — separate Vercel project (recommended)

The **user** site builds from folder **`app`** (e.g. www.jobpool.in). The **admin** dashboard lives in **`admin-temp`** (Next.js app on port 3002 locally). It is **not** included in the `app` build unless you merge projects.

| | User app | Admin app |
|---|----------|-----------|
| **Folder** | `app/` | `admin-temp/` |
| **Vercel Root Directory** | `app` | `admin-temp` |
| **Wallet UPI withdrawals UI** | `/admin/withdrawals` (uses **user** JWT — not for admin APIs) | `/wallet-withdrawals` (uses **admin** JWT after `admin-login`) |

- **Env:** Set `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL` to your API root **including** `/api/v1` (no trailing slash), e.g. `https://api.jobpool.in/api/v1`. Rebuild after changing env.
- Create a **second Vercel project** (same GitHub repo), set **Root Directory** to **`admin-temp`**, production branch **`clean-main`** (or match your admin workflow).
- After each push, **both** projects should build if you want admin changes (including **Wallet Withdrawals** in the sidebar) to go live.
- See also `app/WALLET_API_VERIFICATION.md` for wallet API notes.

## Notes

- Vercel deploys on every push to `clean-main`
- No manual Vercel deploy needed once connected
- If push fails (auth), suggest: `gh auth login` or check remote URL
